## Model card
- **Name:** Big Pickle (free stealth model on OpenCode Zen)
- **Short description:** A free stealth coding/reasoning model served via OpenCode Zen’s OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Its upstream provider is undisclosed; community speculation links it to GLM-5.2 or DeepSeek variants, but no official confirmation exists. Alias: `big-pickle`.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/big-pickle` (chat/completions endpoint). Does not support the Responses API. Base URL: `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Not officially disclosed. First public mentions in late 2025; still available free as of October 2026. Knowledge cutoff unknown.
- **IDs:** `opencode/big-pickle` (no separate “Free” ID; the model itself is free during the stealth period).
- **Context window:** 200,000 tokens (verified via multiple third-party model catalogs). Max output 32,000 tokens. No verified long-context retrieval benchmarks (MRCR/RULER) reported.
- **Modalities:** Text input only; text output. Reasoning: yes. Tool calls: supported. JSON mode: supported. Image/audio/video/PDF input not supported by the model (gateway wrappers may add OCR preprocessing, but the model itself is text-only).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-05):** $0 per 1M input/output tokens (free during stealth period). Free-tier privacy caveat: data may be used for model improvement.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary stealth model; parameters, MoE configuration, and license undisclosed.
